# infrastructure-modules: Ensemble Conventions

Always peer-check 2+ existing ensembles before writing. Prefer ones that touch the same AWS service (e.g. for a Lambda-related ensemble, look at `ensembles/aws-lambda`).

## Required files in every ensemble

- `main.tf` — resources and data lookups
- `variables.tf` — inputs (always include `description`)
- `outputs.tf` — outputs (always include `description`)
- `versions.tf` — provider and Terraform version pins

The repo README says modules MUST NOT include a `terraform {}` block. **This is outdated.** Every active ensemble has `versions.tf` with a `terraform {}` block. Follow the code.

## versions.tf — match recent peers

Floor pins from current peers (use these or newer):

```terraform
terraform {
  required_providers {
    aws = {
      source  = "hashicorp/aws"
      version = "~> 6"
    }
  }
  required_version = ">= 1.2.9"
}
```

- Don't use `required_version = "~> 1"` (too restrictive on minor).
- Don't pin `aws ~> 5` for new ensembles; the repo has moved to `~> 6`.

## Inputs to avoid

- **No `tags` input.** The AWS provider supplies `Owner`/`Billing`/etc. via default tags. Don't accept or apply a `tags` map unless the resource genuinely needs caller-supplied tags beyond the defaults.
- **No `aws_region` input.** Use `data "aws_region" "current" {}` and reference `data.aws_region.current.name`.
- **For VPC, prefer `vpc_name` over `vpc_id`.** Look the VPC up by Name tag so callers don't have to thread the ID through, and so missing VPCs fail at plan time:
  ```terraform
  variable "vpc_name" {
    type        = string
    description = "Name tag of the VPC."
  }

  data "aws_vpc" "this" {
    tags = { Name = var.vpc_name }
  }
  ```
  Pattern reference: `infrastructure-pattern-library/terraform/rds-database/vpc.tf`.

## Egress rules

- Use `aws_vpc_security_group_egress_rule` (not inline `egress` blocks on `aws_security_group`).
- Scope ports to the protocol's real port. **Never use `0-65535` for known protocols.** S3, HTTPS endpoints, etc. → `443` only.

## CI

- Branch name must match `<JIRA-ID>-<kebab>` (e.g. `DE-3396-vrs-lambda-egress-sg`).
- TFLint runs in CI. Don't add a local `.tflint.hcl` to disable rules — fix the code (usually means adding `versions.tf`).
- After merge, the repo auto-tags ensembles. Consumers in `infrastructure-deployments` should reference the tag.
